# Room server host. Leave unset in dev: the app uses <current hostname>:1999,
# so phones on the same Wi-Fi reach your machine's `wrangler dev` server.
# After `npm run party:deploy`, set it to your Worker, for example:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PARTYKIT_HOST=werewolves.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev

# Signing in with the hy13 auth server (OpenID Connect). Both are needed: the
# secret also signs the tickets pages show the room server (lib/ticket.ts).
# Leave unset to turn accounts off, e.g. on Vercel previews whose URLs aren't
# registered redirect URIs.
# AUTH_ISSUER defaults to https://auth.hy13dev.com.
# AUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Stats: finished games go to this Postgres (Neon) database. Set by Vercel's
# Neon integration; locally, `npm run db:migrate` creates the tables. Leave
# unset and nothing is saved (the stats page says so).
# POSTGRES_URL=
